  "question": "You are a graph image parsing assistant.\n\nThe images show an undirected graph at different time steps. Same E* labels indicate the same node across time, and edges are triples [head node, relation type, tail node] where R* is the reusable relation type.\n\nInspect all graph images and reconstruct every graph shown. Do not infer relation meanings or facts that are not visible in the images.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object with this schema:\n{\n  \"graphs\": [\n    {\n      \"graph_id\": \"G1\",\n      \"triples\": [\n        [\"E18\", \"R3\", \"E19\"],\n        [\"E80\", \"\", \"\"]\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n- Preserve every graph ID and keep graph boundaries separate.\n- Extract every node. A node with no incident edge must be emitted as [\"<node label>\", \"\", \"\"]. Replace <node label> with the actual label.\n- Extract every edge as [\"src\", \"relation\", \"dst\"].\n- All graphs are undirected; emit each edge once, and endpoint order is not semantically significant.\n- Preserve node and relation labels exactly.\n- Do not include nodes, directed fields, explanations, Markdown, or any additional keys.",
